WEBVTT

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:05.680
We came up with the concept of the SRS back in 2012, two 1013,

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:09.840
a few of his organisers just chatting over a beer and hey,

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:11.880
why don't we just link our events together and make a

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:14.720
series. It's quite a complicated formula

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:17.760
actually, the SRS. Suddenly on the face of it, it's

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:21.760
a sports competition, but it's got a lot of different dynamics.

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:24.840
You've got to be really careful that what we do in competitions

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:27.440
doesn't destroy the bigger sport outside.

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:30.400
And if you start getting hot, the NCS produced.

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:34.920
How does the general pilot know that this one's intended for

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.760
racing and this one's intended for cross country?

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:41.760
The B category that it's now to be split by the end, it's going

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:47.200
to be low B, high B2 liners just collapse less.

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:51.560
That's it. That's generalized inks, but 95%

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:55.840
of 2 liners are put solid wings that don't collapse, however.

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:10.720
Hello and welcome back to Paragliding Actors.

