comes to aerial sports or the things we can do in the air, you

00:36:04.600 --> 00:36:08.240
know, there's bass, there's skydiving, there's wing suiting,

00:36:08.240 --> 00:36:10.560
there's like different disciplines, speed riding and

00:36:10.560 --> 00:36:12.360
you know, whatever, acro and stuff.

00:36:12.960 --> 00:36:18.240
The only place where we are able to race humans against humans in

00:36:18.240 --> 00:36:20.480
such a large format is paragliding.

00:36:21.200 --> 00:36:22.520
Nothing else. No.

00:36:22.520 --> 00:36:25.680
No other form of entertainment in the air comes even close to

00:36:25.680 --> 00:36:28.000
it. So obviously since there are

00:36:28.000 --> 00:36:31.000
more lives at stake, more resources have to be put in and

00:36:31.000 --> 00:36:35.920
more stringent and norms, which makes sense to masses, have to

00:36:35.920 --> 00:36:40.880
be put in. But EN was a system developed

00:36:41.240 --> 00:36:45.440
quite a long time ago and we have seen that kind of system

00:36:45.440 --> 00:36:51.880
slowly lose it's relevance in in acrobatics, in parachites or in

00:36:51.880 --> 00:36:56.840
speed wings where no matter how long manufacturers tried to

