stick to it or label their wings so that they could educate a

00:37:00.320 --> 00:37:03.480
certain audience, they eventually found it easier to

00:37:03.480 --> 00:37:08.280
give up and have just a loads rating and letting the buck stop

00:37:08.280 --> 00:37:11.280
with the flyer with the user of deciding.

00:37:11.840 --> 00:37:15.160
So now when the user is going out to make a purchase, they

00:37:15.160 --> 00:37:19.920
have this sense of responsibility because nothing

00:37:19.920 --> 00:37:22.520
is being spoken to them about the behaviours and

00:37:22.520 --> 00:37:25.080
characteristics. And then they gauge their own

00:37:25.080 --> 00:37:30.160
decision making accordingly. Are we looking at EN norms

00:37:30.160 --> 00:37:34.560
losing their relevance because we are trying to correct them

00:37:34.560 --> 00:37:39.480
way too much and free flight is anyways about the freedom.

00:37:39.640 --> 00:37:44.120
And is this a sign that EN norms like this is another just

00:37:44.120 --> 00:37:46.120
another way of thinking that I'm looking at, you know, just

00:37:46.120 --> 00:37:49.240
another perspective that may be let people decide themselves and

00:37:49.240 --> 00:37:51.240
just give it a load rating, which is just a safety rating

00:37:51.240 --> 00:37:54.440
that OK, the material won't disintegrate after sort.

00:37:56.400 --> 00:37:58.800
Of I mean, that's another good question.

00:37:58.800 --> 00:38:03.480
So I mean EN first European norm, you've got to remember

