And then on top of that, there are some things that happen like

01:05:38.640 --> 01:05:42.200
Brown's accident. And I think even you guys like

01:05:42.200 --> 01:05:45.520
lost, like he just got lost in Colombia.

01:05:45.520 --> 01:05:49.040
I believe there was a pilot which was never has he been

01:05:49.040 --> 01:05:51.800
found again or like what, what? What was the end result of that?

01:05:52.240 --> 01:05:54.520
No, unfortunately not. So yes, this is one that's

01:05:54.520 --> 01:05:58.920
happened in an SRS last year. We, we had a pilot took off in

01:05:58.920 --> 01:06:04.760
the task and not been seen. I mean it's, it's, we can be

01:06:04.760 --> 01:06:07.000
fairly open on most aspects that happened.

01:06:07.440 --> 01:06:10.120
I don't want to put the pilot down directly too much or

01:06:10.120 --> 01:06:15.480
anything, but the basics were he took off in the task, but he

01:06:15.480 --> 01:06:18.400
wanted to fly something different to the task.

01:06:18.400 --> 01:06:23.000
He wanted to find the direction that we hadn't checked.

01:06:23.000 --> 01:06:26.600
We knew it was just jungle and no roads and no people and no

01:06:26.600 --> 01:06:28.960
phones and nothing. So we would never task that

01:06:28.960 --> 01:06:31.360
direction. We would task in the opposite

01:06:31.360 --> 01:06:35.560
direction, but he'd wanted to fly that area a bit and explore

01:06:35.560 --> 01:06:38.680
it and then probably could run back to the task at a later

01:06:38.680 --> 01:06:41.640
stage. So we have a certain amount of

01:06:41.640 --> 01:06:44.440
tracking that. No, he's not been found

01:06:44.440 --> 01:06:47.760
unfortunately, but there was a set of circumstances after.

01:06:47.760 --> 01:06:50.640
I mean, he did land safely. We did have contact with him

01:06:51.200 --> 01:06:54.600
2428 hours later and he was fined walking back.

01:06:55.720 --> 01:06:58.000
We got location for that. Eventually.

01:06:59.600 --> 01:07:03.200
We had pilot responsibility and as an organiser to create rules

01:07:03.200 --> 01:07:05.520
that everybody will maintain is quite difficult.

01:07:06.080 --> 01:07:10.560
We have a rule now if you take off to fly the task, we must fly

01:07:10.560 --> 01:07:12.680
the task. We mustn't divert off somewhere

01:07:12.680 --> 01:07:14.400
else. We we can't.

01:07:15.200 --> 01:07:17.720
In the old days we had open tasks where you could fly any

01:07:17.720 --> 01:07:20.400
direction. But the sport very quickly

01:07:20.400 --> 01:07:23.640
learnt 30 years ago that that's quite dangerous, having people,

01:07:23.760 --> 01:07:26.600
someone flying 100 KS that way, someone 100 KS that way.

01:07:27.640 --> 01:07:31.200
The format now is we all stay together in a close group.

01:07:32.840 --> 01:07:38.160
I set a task as a task setter, which is guessing the weather 50

01:07:38.160 --> 01:07:40.600
kilometres away, 3 or 4 hours from now.

01:07:41.440 --> 01:07:43.720
It's an educated guess, but it's still a guess.

01:07:44.160 --> 01:07:46.360
But as a group. Then you can radio back to the

01:07:46.360 --> 01:07:49.440
meat director while she'll fly on the task and say hang on, the

01:07:49.440 --> 01:07:53.080
conditions aren't good, this area is not safe, or the pilots

01:07:53.080 --> 01:07:56.400
are mountain terrelli on radio or in a modern system.

01:07:56.400 --> 01:07:59.000
We've got a very advanced tracker system now which we can

01:07:59.000 --> 01:08:04.080
communicate through the trackers and we can stop the task.

01:08:04.320 --> 01:08:06.640
But if you've gone off in a different direction then it's

01:08:06.640 --> 01:08:08.360
very hard for us to allow for that.

01:08:08.360 --> 01:08:13.600
So that there's an aspect there but and that just goes out of

01:08:13.600 --> 01:08:16.560
the whole safety. It's there's no money.

01:08:16.760 --> 01:08:21.520
Most of us are not professional. I'm reasonably professional with

01:08:21.520 --> 01:08:25.439
a lot of stuff I organise, but majority events are run by a

01:08:25.680 --> 01:08:28.880
club as a one off for the year and they look for the volunteers

01:08:28.880 --> 01:08:34.279
